        "title": "exec tool returns images instead of text output (intermittent, deepseek-v4 models)",
        "body": "The exec tool intermittently returns images instead of text command output when used with opencode-go/deepseek-v4-flash models. This makes the tool unreliable for reading command output. All tools (exec, read, write, edit) are affected — they all now return \"(see attached image)\" instead of text. This is a critical bug that renders the agent unable to read ANY output from the system.\n\nSteps to reproduce on 2026-07-05 with OpenClaw 2026.6.11:\n1. Run `exec(command=\"echo hello\")`\n2. Tool returns \"(see attached image)\" instead of \"hello\"\n3. Same for `exec(command=\"pwd\")`, `exec(command=\"whoami\")`\n4. All file tools (read, write, edit) also return images\n5. Behavior is intermittent: sometimes it works, sometimes it doesn't",
